Proton Drive CLI on Gentoo
==========================
This packages the official standalone `proton-drive` executable (with Bun
embedded). Portage owns upgrades; user configuration, sessions, and synced
data remain in upstream XDG locations and are preserved on removal.

Setup and authentication
------------------------
Run as your normal user (sign-in opens a browser):
    proton-drive auth login

Credential storage:
- Default: `libsecret` (requires a running Secret Service provider; installing
  libsecret alone does not start one).
- Terminal/GPG alternative: enable `USE=pass` (`app-admin/pass` — local GPG
  password-store, not Proton Pass `pass-cli`), initialize `pass` with your GPG
  key, and set before login/commands:
      export PROTON_DRIVE_CREDENTIALS_STORE=pass

Note: the upstream amd64 build requires an AVX2-capable CPU.
